  "result": "Rebase almost never on a truly shared branch. Rebase rewrites commit history, so anyone who already pulled it ends up with diverged copies and painful force-push recovery.\n\nRebase OK when:\n- Only you have commits on the branch, nobody else has based work on it.\n- You're updating your feature branch with latest `main` before opening or merging a PR: `git rebase main`.\n- You're cleaning up local, unpushed commits (squash, reword).\n\nUse merge when:\n- Others pull from or push to the branch.\n- You want to preserve true history and avoid force-push.\n\nIf you rebase a pushed branch, use `git push --force-with-lease`, and tell teammates first.",
